  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO: Supporting the Institutional sustainability of AlAqsa Mosque Center for the Restoration of Islamic Manuscipts in Jerusalem: Phase IV: Consolid</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to make of the Center for the Restoration of Islamic Manuscripts of the Haram al-Sharif, in Jerusalem, an operational, autonomous and sustainable entity by the end of the project, and able to safeguard this unique Islamic heritage. The project will include different activities: a Conservation assessment of the Center; the elaboration of conservation and management exit strategy and ten-year vision; the reinforcement of the capacities of the staff; the restoration of the premises; the digitization and inventory of the collections; and the human and material restructuring of the Center. The project will be implemented over an estimated period of three years. The Centre has a restoration and conservation laboratory with essential equipment, facilities and materials. There is a director and 8 staff experienced in the fundamentals of manuscripts conservation, two of whom are more proficient.</narrative>
  </description>
